[369.836619, "o", "\r\nYour Kubernetes control-plane has initialized successfully!\r\n\r\nTo start using your cluster, you need to run the following as a regular user:\r\n\r\n  mkdir -p $HOME/.kube\r\n  sudo cp -i /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf $HOME/.kube/config\r\n  sudo chown $(id -u):$(id -g) $HOME/.kube/config\r\n\r\nAlternatively, if you are the root user, you can run:\r\n\r\n  export KUBECONFIG=/etc/kubernetes/admin.conf\r\n\r\nYou should now deploy a pod network to the cluster.\r\nRun \"kubectl apply -f [podnetwork].yaml\" with one of the options listed at:\r\n  https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/cluster-administration/addons/\r\n\r\n"]
[369.836738, "o", "You can now join any number of the control-plane node running the following command on each as root:\r\n\r\n  kubeadm join controlplaneip:6443 --token am4qcp.8lfqie9tr8t27h8v \\\r\n\t--discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:18bc2959ce9316afc72eaae20b9452e48937e39546be4d975575ad253626705e \\\r\n\t--control-plane --certificate-key b276edff350f85ef8109fc60e1bd3dcab0683ac99d5ca692d7c0d4f52c87c3f3\r\n\r\nPlease note that the certificate-key gives access to cluster sensitive data, keep it secret!\r\nAs a safeguard, uploaded-certs will be deleted in two hours; If necessary, you can use\r\n\"kubeadm init phase upload-certs --upload-certs\" to reload certs afterward.\r\n\r\nThen you can join any number of worker nodes by running the following on each as root:\r\n\r\nkubeadm join controlplaneip:6443 --token am4qcp.8lfqie9tr8t27h8v \\\r\n\t--discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:18bc2959ce9316afc72eaae20b9452e48937e39546be4d975575ad253626705e \r\n"]
[369.839252, "o", "root@master:/home/alkama/k8s-cni-offload/cri-dockerd# \r\n"]
[369.839383, "o", "root@master:/home/alkama/k8s-cni-offload/cri-dockerd# "]
[378.916553, "o", "export KUBECONFIG=/etc/kubernetes/admin.conf\r\n"]
[378.916696, "o", "root@master:/home/alkama/k8s-cni-offload/cri-dockerd# "]
